    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (76.54) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84) serving as our primary offensive engines. **Yordan Alvarez** earns the top efficiency rating by capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Rocker, where his elite 0.469 xwOBA projects massive power output. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Chandler, boosted by a 13% platoon edge and the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which grants him a significant speed advantage in our pursuit of scarce stolen bases. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.81) also demands attention; despite a negative platoon split against Lodolo, his elite speed and top-of-the-order positioning provide an essential boost to our SB category, making him a high-reward start.\n\nDeciding the final bench spots required navigating a congested middle-infield and outfield. **Luke Raley** (44.34) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly missing the cutoff due to an unfavorable park factor and a less efficient projection compared to **Kyle Schwarber** (57.99) or **Junior Caminero** (52.12). While **Luke Raley** offers respectable platoon value, the optimizer prioritized the higher ceiling of **Junior Caminero** despite his tougher assignment against Gilbert. We are also monitoring several weather alerts; the 45% rain risk for **Caleb Durbin** and the 39% chance affecting **Pete Crow-Armstrong** are notable, though their respective efficiency scores remain high enough to warrant starting them as we preserve our game caps.\n\nFinally, we are managing risk where the matchup difficulty is highest. **Dillon Dingler** (47.02) and **Casey Schmitt** (45.79) are hovering near our performance floor; while they remain in the lineup due to the scarcity of high-tier alternatives, their production is hindered by elite-level opposing starters like S\u00e1nchez and Freeland. We have excluded **Carson Benge** (35.80) entirely, as his dismal sub-40 score against a dominant 1.50 xERA arm represents a liability to our daily efficiency. With **Kazuma Okamoto**\u2019s lineup status still pending, we will remain vigilant to ensure his confirmed slot in the three-hole, as any shift down the order would trigger a re-evaluation of his current 53.88 efficiency rating.",
